th evidence","context_item_id":"constraint:0003:922449192924884e","item_digest":"dbb94ffe2c16c2720b6ed8fcab572368dc40d247a864f36de18a9797406bba12","item_kind":"constraint","mandatory":true,"relevance_basis":"declared-request-constraint","schema_version":"are.context-item/v1","source_digest":"922449192924884e08c759df8963f85e8665cf20e3e559c5d752b7fee15d9d67","source_ref":"request:req-20260912-formal-runtimes-wsl-015","temporal_scope":"turn","transform_refs":["context-basis/v1"]},{"authority_effect":"none","authority_posture":"candidate-nonauthorizing-codex-context","content":"use exact pinned runtime versions and verify cryptographic digests","context_item_id":"constraint:0004:b8c1202dca4e9b07","item_digest":"6ca4cdf3ec2acdcc74f05be8cd8f1aaaad3e2d7f526d06393ea89018be18ca7a","item_kind":"constraint","mandatory":true,"relevance_basis":"declared-request-constraint","schema_version":"are.context-item/v1","source_digest":"b8c1202dca4e9b07103ab3fe1cd3d04a11c0732f1a038d5f33accda6f97a44a3","source_ref":"request:req-20260912-formal-runtimes-wsl-015","temporal_scope":"turn","transform_refs":["context-basis/v1"]},{"authority_effect":"none","authority_posture":"active","content":{"definition_id":"CAV2-D49","text":"Normative Definition:\nClosed authority-kind enumeration is the invariant that the set of authority\n**kinds** is a closed enumeration (the `../AUTHORITY-MODEL.md` Authority Kinds\ntable). An artifact whose kind is **not** in that enumeration may not acquire or\nexercise authority — it defaults to **blocked** pending an owner decision that adds\nthe kind to the enumeration with its declared lifecycle (`CAV2-D48`) and owner\nroute. Adding a kind is itself owner-gated.\n\nPlain-Language Intuition:\nA new *type* of authority can't start governing just because it appeared. Until it\nis on the official list of kinds — with its lifecycle and owner — anything of that\nkind is blocked.\n\nDomain-Context Voice:\nThis definition **names** the closure invariant. As of 2026-06-23 it is **enacted\nin review mode**: a **default-deny catch-all row** was added to the\n[AUTHORITY-MODEL Authority Kinds table](../AUTHORITY-MODEL.md#authority-kinds) by\ndecision-gate ([decision record](../decisions/2026-06-23-authority-kind-closure-catchall-row.md)),\nso an unenumerated kind defaults to blocked. The **deterministic** enforcement (the\nautomated kind-enumeration scan, the former `CAV2-C16` validator) is still pending\n(OQ-1). Per the OQ-2 recommendation, the kind-table amendment for `invariant`/`axiom`\nas their own kinds stays a future decision-gate call (they currently govern as the\n`Definition` kind).\n\nBoundary:\nScoped to authority **kinds** (the enumeration), not individual artifacts (that is\nthe Authority Rule, `CAV2-D41`) and not the per-artifact promotion path (`CAV2-D48`\n+ the promotion-policy ladder). Promoting this definition did not by itself enact\nthe kind table as closed-with-default-deny. Review-mode enactment now lives in\nthe [AUTHORITY-MODEL catch-all row](../AUTHORITY-MODEL.md#authority-kinds);\ndeterministic enforcement remains pending.","version_or_revision":"2230d77ec302312bd892bf6149e77d1d905701a367972b77411eeca103e868fe"},"context_item_id":"definition:CAV2-D49","item_digest":"0f758c417d3188f7c05a69643a8f38517988f5d955d46de2bb257d0b83c2a3fd","item_kind":"definition","mandatory":true,"relevance_basis":"request-term-match","schema_version":"are.context-item/v1","source_digest":"2230d77ec302312bd892bf6149e77d1d905701a367972b77411eeca103e868fe","source_ref":"cyberAlchemy-v2/authority/definitions/DEFINITIONS.md#concept:CAV2-D49","temporal_scope":"source-epoch","transform_refs":["definition-closure/v1"]},{"authority_effect":"none","authority_posture":"active","content":{"definition_id":"CAV2-D57","text":"Normative Definition:\nExact publication authorization is the CyberAlchemy v2 rule that private\nmaterial may cross a publication boundary only after two separate decisions:\n\n1. every source owner authorizes an exact candidate slice, its allowed claims,\n   audience, channel, privacy policies, and requested publishing principal; and\n2. after private generation and privacy validation, that publishing principal\n   approves the exact final output bytes, digest, audience, channel, and claim\n   ceiling.\n\nThe first decision permits creation and review of a private publication\ncandidate. It does not permit unknown future bytes to be published. The second\ndecision applies only to the exact output it binds. Any change to the sources,\nclaims, policies, generator, output bytes, audience, channel, or publishing\nprincipal requires the applicable decisions to be repeated.\n\nAll material is private by default when no valid exact authorization exists.\nGeneration, validation, proof, obligation discharge, CAV2 promotion, or domain\nadoption does not grant publication permission.\n\nPlain-Language Intuition:\nPermission to prepare a public draft is not permission to publish it. Owners\nfirst approve the ingredients and limits; a publisher later approves the exact\nfinished file and destination.\n\nDomain-Context Voice:\nIn CyberAlchemy v2 this definition keeps the private authority spine and its\ndomain evidence private while still allowing a later, deliberately bounded\npublic explanation or result. A generated documentation page remains a private\nprojection until both decisions exist. Public Arcanum receives no private prose,\nproof internals, engine mechanisms, research, or validation material merely\nbecause a generator or checker succeeded.\n\nBoundary:\nExact publication authorization is not classification authority, adoption,\npromotion, proof, truth, freshness, privacy validation, deployment, or release by\nitself. It does not create a universal classification vocabulary: each source\nowner retains its own meanings, and a projection carries exact owner-qualified\nreferences without reinterpreting them. It authorizes no present public output;\nevery actual publication still needs exact permissions and a boundary-crossing\nreceipt.","version_or_revision":"96210640607960fc955c9e902cb66f9fbe549b115f8b66f8786f9e8e0978bc42"},"context_item_id":"definition:CAV2-D57","item_digest":"bddf729dab61f64980957d7d93e1a584ba3b41a18e30537a5a0cb57aaf2dcf06","item_kind":"definition","mandatory":true,"relevance_basis":"request-term-match","schema_version":"are.context-item/v1","source_digest":"96210640607960fc955c9e902cb66f9fbe549b115f8b66f8786f9e8e0978bc42","source_ref":"cyberAlchemy-v2/authority/definitions/DEFINITIONS.md#concept:CAV2-D57","temporal_scope":"source-epoch","transform_refs":["definition-closure/v1"]},{"authority_effect":"none","authority_posture":"repository-instruction","content":{"instruction_id":"repository-root-agents","text":"# CyberAlchemy v2 Agent Instructions\n\nThis project is staged inside the private `domainspec-core` umbrella. Parent\nrepository submodule discipline still applies.\n\n## Local Authority Model\n\n- Canonical local definitions source:\n  [authority/definitions/DEFINITIONS.md](authority/definitions/DEFINITIONS.md)\n- Definitions lookup:\n  [authority/definitions/DEFINITIONS-INDEX.md](authority/definitions/DEFINITIONS-INDEX.md)\n- Authority import ledgers:\n  [authority/imports/README.md](authority/imports/README.md)\n- Stable repository constitution:\n  [authority/constitutions/STABLE-REPOSITORY-CONSTITUTION.md](authority/constitutions/STABLE-REPOSITORY-CONSTITUTION.md)\n- Project discipline catalog:\n  [disciplines/DISCIPLINES.md](disciplines/DISCIPLINES.md)\n- Source map:\n  [SOURCE-MAP.md](SOURCE-MAP.md)\n\nNarrative, research, observability, inventory, ontology, and ops artifacts may\nexplain these surfaces, but they do not redefine them.\n\n## Working Rules\n\n- Keep source evidence linked by path. Do not copy large upstream documents into\n  this project unless a later import plan requires it.\n- Stage scattered definitions, glossaries, constitutions, axioms, quality rules,\n  and anti-patterns under `authority/imports/` before promoting them.\n- Treat [../.arcanum/inventory/](../.arcanum/inventory/) and\n  [../.arcanum/ontology-vault/](../.arcanum/ontology-vault/) as read models and\n  candidate maps, not promoted authority.\n- Keep public Arcanum patterns separate from private DomainSpec evidence.\n- Generated runtime mirrors are evidence of projection, not canonical source.\n- Research may propose; authority decides; implementation waits for a gate.\n- Every durable informational artifact should carry an Open Questions section or\n  link to the artifact that owns its unresolved questions.\n\n## Agent Routing\n\nEvery request begins at `CA2-ROUTE-ENTRY`. Load these three bootstrap files:\n\n- [Routing profile](agent-routing/profile.json)\n- [Route registry](agent-routing/routes.json)\n- [Router contract](agent-routing/ROUTER.md)\n\nThe registry is the single repository objective router. Select exactly one\nnon-entry route and announce its `read_first` list before reading it. Follow\nits lifecycle state, authorization requirements, write ceiling, and blockers.\nIf the objective cannot be resolved unambiguously, use `CA2-ROUTE-AMBIGUOUS`\nand ask for the smallest missing decision. Do not introduce routing fallbacks.\n\nAfter the bootstrap reads, call the local ARE CLI to evaluate the request:\n`node implementation/agent-reasoning-engine/bin/are.mjs decide route`, with\none JSON request on stdin. Follow the exact\n[CLI contract](agent-routing/capabilities/are-cli/README.md) and\n[request schema](agent-routing/capabilities/are-cli/request.schema.json).\nPreserve the user's raw text, mark inferred objective fields, and use distinct\ncaller session/request IDs. ARE evaluates the registry; it does not replace it.\nUse the returned route contract for selection. Carry its receipt into `context`,\n`effect` at consequential boundaries, and `continue` at completion boundaries.\nThese calls grant no effects and do not erase existing user authorization.\nEngine/source failures are explicit diagnostics, never alternate routing.\n\nWhen the user expresses an intention to start an unbounded new product,\nproject, system, capability, workflow, or initiative, label the objective\n`define-intake` rather than inferring Plan or Implement. Route it through\n`CA2-ROUTE-DEFINE` and use the Define process to elicit and confirm the user's\ndomain language, scope, desired outcome, consumers, distinctions, constraints,\nowners, and open questions. Do not relabel an explicit implementation request\nfor an already-bounded target. A Definition Pack remains candidate evidence;\nroute any later Plan or Implement request separately.\n\nUse `CA2-ROUTE-LOCATE` and the [project index](agent-routing/project-index.json)\nto resolve user-cited names before asking for paths. For explicitly scoped `../domainspec-core` lookup, use\n`CA2-ROUTE-DOMAINSPEC-CORE` and its\n[sibling inventory](agent-routing/DOMAINSPEC-CORE-INDEX.md). When recent work is\nrelevant, use `CA2-ROUTE-RECENT` for bounded committed context, then return to\nthe original objective route. Keep uncommitted work distinct from that history.\n\nRoute availability, runtime availability, and governance admission are separate.\nCarry forward the `CAV2-D65` construction chain for implementation-bearing work;\nroute selection does not grant authority or authorize effects.\n\n### Ontology-runtime enforcement suspension\n\nThe candidate ontology runtime is not a mandatory repository prerequisite.\nDirect diagnostic calls use `CA2-ROUTE-ONTOLOGY`; other work declares its exact\nrecord and selector dependencies under the selected objective route. Mandatory\nenforcement requires a separately selected and validated Rust governance binding.\n\n## Native development toolchain\n\nFor Rust/C/C++ builds, use `tools/toolchain/run <command>` from this checkout,\nor its absolute path from another working directory. The launcher supplies\nCargo, GCC and the linker without relying on login-shell configuration. See\n[tools/toolchain/README.md](tools/toolchain/README.md) for the version lock,\ninstallation and `doctor.py` verification. Preserve nested Rust toolchain pins;\ndo not invent per-test paths or install another temporary compiler.\n\n## Open Questions\n\nRouting questions are owned by the [router package](agent-routing/README.md),\n[project lookup contract](agent-routing/PROJECT-LOOKUP.md), and\n[recent-context capability](agent-routing/capabilities/recent-context/README.md).\n"},"context_item_id":"instruction:repository-root-agents","item_digest":"e7cbefd7143601916c9566a87c6e5b84c0f15659b09c9ad73dedf1c39bfd459e","item_kind":"repository-instruction","mandatory":true,"relevance_basis":"repository-scope-instruction","schema_version":"are.context-item/v1","source_digest":"4c6f8362136ebcaeeac1624bc42e3610584e1fb09a7b635495f28d7347b299ef","source_ref":"cyberAlchemy-v2/AGENTS.md","temporal_scope":"source-epoch","transform_refs":["exact-text-projection/v1"]},{"authority_effect":"none","authority_posture":"basis-posture","content":{"edge_id":"agent-reasoning-engine.edge.context-assembly-creates-envelope","edge_type":"creates","from_node_id":"agent-reasoning-engine.ContextAssembly","to_node_id":"agent-reasoning-engine.ContextEnvelope"},"context_item_id":"ontology-edge:agent-reasoning-engine.edge.context-assembly-creates-envelope","item_digest":"fab67a9c490f5b4bddfdc6363f72260ece3b928b7406ba12bb5eb62a022b7714","item_kind":"ontology-edge","mandatory":true,"relevance_basis":"declared-or-recursively-required-edge","schema_version":"are.context-item/v1","source_digest":"e9b2544b9c76d42c5a18492e89d76f648eb88024253ce68ece08a422c97e87e7","source_ref":"ontology#edge:agent-reasoning-engine.edge.context-assembly-creates-envelope","temporal_scope":"source-epoch","transform_refs":["lock/v1"]},{"authority_effect":"none","authority_posture":"basis-posture","content":{"edge_id":"agent-reasoning-engine.edge.context-assembly-reads-context-item","edge_type":"reads","from_node_id":"agent-reasoning-engine.ContextAssembly","to_node_id":"agent-reasoning-engine.ContextItem"},"context_item_id":"ontology-edge:agent-reasoning-engine.edge.context-assembly-reads-context-item","item_digest":"43a3aa0cd0357c8ba06a72b81b87fd81e0257fdcb73a15479746687cfc16825f","item_kind":"ontology-edge","mandatory":true,"relevance_basis":"declared-or-recursively-required-edge","schema_version":"are.context-item/v1","source_digest":"ec5444bf313baa81d4897837b188c93f2708ff90890433a0607545ef2ac84afa","source_ref":"ontology#edge:agent-reasoning-engine.edge.context-assembly-reads-context-item","temporal_scope":"source-epoch","transform_refs":["lock/v1"]},{"authority_effect":"none","authority_posture":"basis-posture","content":{"intent":"Select and freeze only context that is relevant to the bounded request and its declared evidence obligations while recording exclusions and gaps.","node_id":"agent-reasoning-engine.ContextAssembly","node_type":"Operation"},"context_item_id":"ontology-node:agent-reasoning-engine.ContextAssembly","item_digest":"7154c782fa5f156a4fdbe87f3263aa0f3a3f90b5b83bea9980f90485632052bf","item_kind":"ontology-node","mandatory":true,"relevance_basis":"declared-initial-node","schema_version":"are.context-item/v1","source_digest":"bba0ad94b28fb314459047172ba0a623f1d60f7d368f82a24477bf1e856d740f","source_ref":"ontology#node:agent-reasoning-engine.ContextAssembly","temporal_scope":"source-epoch","transform_refs":["lock/v1"]},{"authority_effect":"none","authority_posture":"basis-posture","content":{"intent":"Freeze the included and excluded context, dependency identities, contradictions, gaps, freshness state, and claim ceiling for one reasoning run.","node_id":"agent-reasoning-engine.ContextEnvelope","node_type":"Entity"},"context_item_id":"ontology-node:agent-reasoning-engine.ContextEnvelope","item_digest":"1c36b2492e0433ead48343d6005eb42f860dec445da677346839d53d18839718","item_kind":"ontology-node","mandatory":true,"relevance_basis":"required-edge-endpoint","schema_version":"are.context-item/v1","source_d